The Government recognises that data centres are a critical component of Ireland's digital infrastructure and play an important role in supporting economic activity, public services and the wider digital economy.
The Government's policy position is set out in the Government Statement on the Role of Data Centres in Ireland's Enterprise Strategy, published in July 2022. The Statement seeks to align Ireland's digital and green transitions and recognises that, given electricity system constraints and decarbonisation requirements, future data centre development must deliver strong economic benefits while supporting national climate and energy objectives.
Under this policy, the Government has a preference for data centre developments that:
• are associated with strong economic activity and employment;
• make efficient use of electricity grid infrastructure;
• support additional renewable energy generation;
• have a clear pathway to decarbonisation and net-zero operation; and
• provide wider benefits for communities and enterprise.
Consistent with the Government Statement on the Role of Data Centres in Ireland's Enterprise Strategy and the Programme for Government 2025 - Securing Ireland's Future, the Government supports sustainable data centre development that contributes to economic growth and digitalisation while remaining compatible with security of electricity supply and Ireland's climate objectives.
