The Programme for Government and the revised National Development Plan set out an ambitious agenda for Building our Shared Island, backed by a total €2 billion commitment to the Shared Island Fund out to 2035. We are forging ahead with this investment and cooperation agenda across all sectors.
On 23 June, the Government made a funding commitment of over €377m from the Shared Island Fund to resource 12 new projects to be delivered as part of the Initiative over 2027-2030. This includes:
- €193 million for improved rail infrastructure and travel times between Dublin, Belfast and Derry;
- €35 million for the continuation of the hourly frequency service to Belfast out to 2030;
- €14 million investment in Offshore Renewable Energy servicing facilities at eligible ports North and South; and,
- A €3.5 million contribution to cricket grounds development in Belfast as part of joint hosting by Ireland and the UK of the T20 Men’s Cricket World Cup in 2030.
There are also Shared Island Fund contributions to enable major new cooperation programmes out to 2030 on:
- Water Quality in Lough Neagh Catchment areas North and South;
- Early Years Education;
- Digital Creative Industries;
- Industrial Sustainability;
- A new Support Centre as part of Northwest Cancer Centre at Altnagelvin; and
- Tourism product development and a docklands bridges delivery partnership.
